== new findings (PLAN text only, all MINOR) ==
[MINOR] F-D-01 (PLAN.md section 4.1): Section 4.1 uses illustrative event families that do not match the published contract event names: `inventory.transaction.posted`, `purchase_order.`, `item_receipt.`. The contracts define po.created/approved/receipted/billed/closed (FS-08), inventory.receipt.posted|reversed (FS-08/FS-04), inventory.committed.changed, inventory.fulfilled and inventory.issued (FS-04).
[MINOR] F-D-02 (PLAN.md section 4.1): Section 4.1 says every state-changing step posts synchronously to the inventory ledger. ARCHITECTURE 2.3 defines non-posting control commands C-01..C-06 (commitments, TO approve/close, WO void) and document/approval state machines that never append ledger rows; only inventory-quantity/value-affecting steps post.
[MINOR] F-D-03 (PLAN.md section 4.1): Section 4.1 states the runbook (section 7) requires a golden end-to-end workflow pass before a wave is promoted, but section 7 contains no such requirement: its per-set workflow runs one golden-path smoke transaction (section 5 deployment-protocol step 4) and wave closure uses the section 6 exit criteria. Either add the requirement to the runbook or reword section 4.1 as a recommendation.
[MINOR] F-D-04 (PLAN.md section 6.1): Section 6.1 states the sizing as 8 x L, 6 x M, 2 x S, but FEATURE-SETS section 1 (the per-set size authority) is 7 x L, 7 x M, 2 x S (16 sets total). Correct the distribution in the PLAN sentence.

